    story1: 'The German army sent its orders with the **Enigma** and was sure nobody could break it. Nobody in Poland had seen inside the army Enigma. And yet a 27-year-old mathematician, **Marian Rejewski**, worked out how the wires ran inside its rotors: from intercepted messages, from mathematics, and from a few documents obtained by French intelligence.',
