    stripIn: 'letter', stripOut: 'after the plugboard',
    twiceTitle: 'The current goes through the plugboard twice',
    twiceText: 'On the wheels the plugboard is a ring on the black wheel, under the rotors (page 5). The current goes through it twice: at the start from the key to the right rotor, at the end from the right rotor to the lamp. A coloured letter on the ring is the cable’s other end, in the same colour as the cable on the panel.',
    ownTitle: 'Your plugboard: draw the cables with crayons',
    plugNote: v => `The Germans added the plugboard in 1930. With ${v.nCables} cables it can be set up in **${v.ways}** ways. The plugboard only renames letters, so at first the Polish mathematicians could leave it out. Later you can write your own cables on the empty plugboard on page 10.`,
