    blankOver: 'FOR THE KEEN · CUT-OUT', blankTitle: 'An empty plugboard', blankSub: 'Set your own cables and code a message for a friend.',
    blankHowTitle: 'How to write in the cables',
    blankSteps: ['Choose your cables. In 1932 the Germans used 6 cables, but you can take from 1 to 13. You can draw them first on the empty panel on page 7.', 'For each cable, e.g. A–B: over the black A write B, and over the black B write A.', 'Write nothing over letters without a cable: there the current goes straight down.', 'Cut out the ring and put it on the black wheel instead of today’s plugboard. Whoever decodes needs the same plugboard and the same window.'],
    blankNote: 'Check: every letter you wrote has a partner. If B stands over A, then A must stand over B, and no letter has two cables.',

    missionStamp: 'MISSION', missionTitle: 'The cipher clerk’s exam',
